      "hook": "You said sorry three times before lunch today.",
      "explain": "Psychologists call it the fawn response. Your nervous system says sorry to keep the peace. You apologize for things that were never your fault. Saying sorry first feels safer than being blamed.",
      "reframe": "That reflex isn't weakness, it's a survival skill you learned. Somewhere you were taught that taking blame kept you safe. You're allowed to take up space without an apology. Save your sorry for when you truly mean it.",
